<!--
  This file selects and maps existing parameters to logical addresses that
  fits CANopen.
  The XML elements and attributes:
  <Product PartNumber="" CustomerSpecific="" Name="" ErrorCheck=""
   The root element
    Attribute: PartNumber
     The attribute contains the partnumber of the final binary image. The
     partnumber value is also used as tag name in Subversion.
    Attribute: Name
     The attribute contains the user friendly name that matches the PartNumber.
    Attribute: ErrorCheck
     The attribute is used to control what to do when a Group or a
     Member definition can not be found. Values can be 'true' or 'false'.
     If you use ErrorCheck="false" then you can check the automatically
     generated missing.txt file for all missing objects. When "true" all
     entries in the addressmap.xml file must be found.
     It also controls the automatic generation of version information.
     When ErrorCheck="true" then new version information is automatically
     generated, forcing some files to always be rebuild.
     (This was previously controlled using Release/Debug).
    Attribute: CustomerSpecific:
     An optional value that can be used by application code.
  <Includes>
   Contains all system and application pre processor macros.
  <Version OriginalPlasmaLabel="">
    Attribute: OriginalPlasmaLabel
     The attribute contains the PLASMA label and shall only be changed when
     a new PLASMA version is made (only by R&D SW).
  <Hardware>
   ???
    Attribute: SWToHWCompatibilityNumber
     ???
  <ReplaceList>
   A list of compatible application software based on part number.
   <Replaces PartNumber="" />
    Attribute: PartNumber
     Part number of software that can be replaced.
  <AddressMap>
   See description below
  Scudo CAN Artno:  69G21003V00x00-trunk
  Getz Artno:   69G32001V01
  EUCAR Artno: 69H06001V00
-->
