        <Event Name="LoadActiveWhenODOffCh1" EventId="1121u" CheckIn4Khz="FALSE" StoreInLog="TRUE" StoreFreezeFrame="FALSE">
      <Description><![CDATA[
        
        <b>Description</b><br/>
        When high-side in is high, the voltage drop across the load should be inactive
        (i.e. OD & HS voltage is at the same level) if the state of the OD & HS swtiches
        is exclusively off or both off.  <br/>
        This event is triggered if the voltage drop is active across the load when OD is off.
        It inidicates that the open drain has short circuit to B- <br/>
        <b>When is event evaluated</b><br/>
        When high-side In is high and OD is off. <br/>
        <b>Related parameters</b><br/>
        No related parameters.
        
      ]]></Description>
